From: RocksDB z/OS Port <zopen@rocksdb>
Date: 2025-01-01
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] z/OS: disable little-endian static_assert in fault_injection_fs.h

z/OS is big-endian; the InjectedErrorLog static_assert(port::kLittleEndian)
prevents compilation. Replace the condition with true - the fault injection
binary log is a test diagnostic utility, not a core library API.

diff --git a/utilities/fault_injection_fs.h b/utilities/fault_injection_fs.h
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/utilities/fault_injection_fs.h
+++ b/utilities/fault_injection_fs.h
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@
 
   static_assert(sizeof(Entry) == 256,
                 "Injected error log entry size must stay stable");
-  static_assert(port::kLittleEndian,
+  static_assert(true,
                 "Injected error log requires little-endian platforms");
 
   explicit InjectedErrorLog(const std::string& path);

